    {
      "cluster_id": 4,
      "headline_hint": "Election Commission issues SIR notices to millions of Delhi voters, prompting political reaction",
      "section": "india",
      "batch_position": 0,
      "claim_count": 17,
      "distinct_outlets": 5,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 17
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 34,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Not being mapped to the previous Special Intensive Revision (SIR) accounted for 42% of the notices issued to voters on Delhi's draft electoral roll.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/name-mismatch-age-difference-and-more-why-3-3-million-voters-in-delhi-received-ec-notices-after-sir-bid-in-capital-101789954533654.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Name mismatches with the previous electoral roll accounted for 41% of SIR notices issued in Delhi, with parent name mismatches comprising 24% and self-name mismatches comprising 17%.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/name-mismatch-age-difference-and-more-why-3-3-million-voters-in-delhi-received-ec-notices-after-sir-bid-in-capital-101789954533654.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Discrepancies in age differences accounted for 16% of the SIR notices issued in Delhi.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/name-mismatch-age-difference-and-more-why-3-3-million-voters-in-delhi-received-ec-notices-after-sir-bid-in-capital-101789954533654.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "A total of 59,791 SIR notices issued to voters in Delhi had no reason listed against them.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/name-mismatch-age-difference-and-more-why-3-3-million-voters-in-delhi-received-ec-notices-after-sir-bid-in-capital-101789954533654.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Shyam Mukhija, aged 125 from Sadar Bazar assembly constituency in Old Delhi, was the oldest person served an SIR notice due to a self-name mismatch.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/name-mismatch-age-difference-and-more-why-3-3-million-voters-in-delhi-received-ec-notices-after-sir-bid-in-capital-101789954533654.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Notices were issued to 34.5% of men, 33.4% of women, and 50% of transgender individuals on Delhi's draft electoral roll.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Hindustan Times",
          "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/name-mismatch-age-difference-and-more-why-3-3-million-voters-in-delhi-received-ec-notices-after-sir-bid-in-capital-101789954533654.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "More than 80.62 lakh voter names were deleted from draft rolls after being marked as shifted or absent, but only 6.66 lakh Form-6 applications were submitted for inclusion.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/bangalore/sir-against-8062-lakh-shifted-absent-names-only-666-lakh-form-6-applications/article71488325.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "During the SIR process in Bihar, the total electorate decreased from 7.89 crore to about 7.42 crore despite 21.53 lakh electors being added through Form-6 applications.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/bangalore/sir-against-8062-lakh-shifted-absent-names-only-666-lakh-form-6-applications/article71488325.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Prominent political and official figures served SIR notices in Delhi include LK Advani, Jagdeep Dhankhar, S Jaishankar, Sukhbir Singh Sandhu, Manish Sisodia, and Delhi Chief Minister Rekha Gupta.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/delhi/lk-advani-dhankar-sisodia-also-issued-sir-notices/articleshow/134372553.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Deceased former chairman of the Economic Advisory Council to the Prime Minister Bibek Debroy was issued an SIR notice as his name appeared on the flagged draft rolls.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/delhi/lk-advani-dhankar-sisodia-also-issued-sir-notices/articleshow/134372553.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "The Delhi Chief Electoral Officer's office stated that disposal of notices will be completed by October 29, 2026, and the final electoral roll will be published on November 4, 2026.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/delhi/lk-advani-dhankar-sisodia-also-issued-sir-notices/articleshow/134372553.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Lawyer Kapil Sibal described the Special Intensive Revision as a 'special intensive deletion' aimed at removing valid voters.",
          "kind": "quote",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/delhi/lk-advani-dhankar-sisodia-also-issued-sir-notices/articleshow/134372553.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "The Election Commission of India launched the Special Intensive Revision exercise in Delhi on May 14.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/delhi-sir-got-an-ec-notice-ceo-says-names-won-t-be-automatically-deleted-after-advani-jaishankar-among-those-flagged-11789913825204.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "cluster_id": 4,
          "text": "Authorities in Delhi received 84,263 Form-6 applications for voter inclusion between August 31 and September 19, following 2,12,400 applications received up to August 30.",
